# File: tests/features/hub-provider-visibility.feature
# Generated from: specs/38-hide-providers-without-a-login-from-the-model-hub/requirements.md
Feature: Hide providers without a login from the /model hub

  @SCN001
  Scenario: A provider without a login has no hub entry
    Given "xai" is enabled, needs an API key login, and has no stored login
    When the person opens the "/model" hub
    Then the sidebar has no "xAI" entry
    And no "xai/" model appears in "All models" or in a search for "xai"

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Logged-in and login-free providers still appear
    Given "opencode-go" has a stored login and another enabled provider needs no login
    When the person opens the "/model" hub
    Then the sidebar lists "All models", "Claude", "OpenCode Go" and the login-free provider
    And both providers' models are listed

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Logging in makes the provider appear
    Given "xai" was hidden because it had no stored login
    When the person completes "/login" for "xai" and opens the "/model" hub again
    Then the sidebar lists "xAI" and its models

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Logging out hides the provider
    Given "opencode-go" is listed in the hub with one stored login
    When the person runs "/logout" for "opencode-go" and opens the "/model" hub again
    Then the sidebar has no "OpenCode Go" entry

  @SCN005
  Scenario: A stored but failing login keeps the provider listed
    Given "opencode-go" has a stored login whose credential cannot currently be resolved
    And the catalog keeps its cached models
    When the person opens the "/model" hub
    Then the sidebar lists "OpenCode Go" with its cached models

  @SCN006
  Scenario: Nothing replaces the hidden entries
    Given no login-requiring provider has a stored login
    When the person opens the "/model" hub
    Then the sidebar lists only "All models" and "Claude"
    And the hub shows the Claude models with no "has no credentials" text, no login button and no hint about hidden providers
